WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.213
Scaled copies, dilations, similar figures, and slope are really one idea: changing a shape's size without changing its shape.

2
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.123
This triangle has sides three, four, and five.

3
00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:16.131
Multiply every side by two, and you get six, eight, and ten.

4
00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:19.404
That's a scaled copy, with a scale factor of two.

5
00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:21.274
And the angles don't change.

6
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:24.927
Stretch it only sideways, and the angles change.

7
00:00:24.927 --> 00:00:26.651
That's not a scaled copy.

8
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.728
Scale drawings work the same way.

9
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:35.804
One inch to fifty feet means every inch on the drawing stands for fifty feet in real life.

10
00:00:35.804 --> 00:00:38.167
So four inches is two hundred feet.

11
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:42.720
A dilation grows or shrinks a figure from a center point.

12
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.593
With a scale factor of two, every point moves twice as far from the center.

13
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:50.651
With one half, every point is half as far.

14
00:00:50.651 --> 00:00:55.699
Bigger than one grows, less than one shrinks, and exactly one changes nothing.

15
00:00:56.533 --> 00:01:00.675
With the center at the origin, just multiply both coordinates.

16
00:01:00.675 --> 00:01:03.147
Two, one, times three, is six, three.

17
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:11.185
Two figures are similar if translations, rotations, reflections, and dilations take one onto the other.

18
00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:14.821
The angles match, and the sides keep the same ratio.

19
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:20.505
Slope tells how steep a line is: vertical change over horizontal change.

20
00:01:20.505 --> 00:01:25.544
This slope triangle goes up two and over three, so the slope is two thirds.

21
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:30.243
A bigger slope triangle is just a dilation: up four, over six.

22
00:01:30.243 --> 00:01:31.438
Still two thirds.

23
00:01:31.438 --> 00:01:36.571
Slope triangles on a line are always similar, so the slope never changes.

24
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:38.393
That gives us a test.

25
00:01:38.393 --> 00:01:40.361
Is nine, seven on this line?

26
00:01:40.361 --> 00:01:43.102
From zero, one, it's up six, over nine.

27
00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:46.687
Six ninths is two thirds, so yes, it's on the line.

28
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:50.980
And if a line goes down to the right, its slope is negative.

29
00:01:51.817 --> 00:01:59.127
Remember: scale factors multiply lengths, similar figures have the same shape, and slope is rise over run.

30
00:01:59.127 --> 00:02:00.713
Good luck on your test!
